From c1f9a18c3816408db7f64977db4f9f3ec01fda17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stop automatic retries after provider content
 refusal [daveey]

A provider content-safety refusal is a stop-for-review outcome, never a
provider routing input. Use the existing shared classify_failure function
for accounting and notices; recognize the authentic cybersecurity refusal
message, force the first charged failure through gave_up/triage, retain
sticky operator review, and leave normal crash retries unchanged.

Canonical notices identify provider, model, run and the first 200 message
characters, state that it is not a worker crash and will not auto-retry,
and direct manual review/re-scoping or archival. Exclude refusals from
systemic worker-crash fix-card creation. No routing/pin changes.

Why-chain:
1. The provider refused guard/sandbox work; ev1957427 worker_output records
   its content-safety message (14 such failures in the observed week).
2. Dispatch treated the refusal as a crash, charged it, and retried it;
   ev1956924 was followed by respawn ev1957047-1957048.
3. Failure finalization had no refusal outcome and eventually exhausted
   the crash budget with transient/worker_failures_exhausted (ev1957428).
4. The notice classifier was not used for the finalizer decision; its
   regex also missed the exact cybersecurity-flagged provider message.
5. No dispatcher regression pinned first-refusal no-retry behavior.
Root happened: safety refusals and worker crashes shared crash policy.
Root not caught: only notice/manual guidance, not end-to-end tests.

Proof: authentic ev1957427 fixture RED on main (ready != triage), GREEN
with first-failure charge, canonical notice, no second sweep, sticky
triage, ordinary two-failure budget, primary release decision, and
unchanged ready/review ratio routing. A three-refusal RED/GREEN pair
also proves no systemic crash fix card is spawned.

Board-primary note: core sends force_trip=true, block_kind=capability,
and extra.reason_code=provider_refusal. The external Board transition
currently overwrites this reason code and needs its companion authority
change before the canonical primary-path acceptance is fully satisfied.

